  "title": "CHAPTER 6: CYBER SECURITY",
  "order": 6,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "91beqwo",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6.1 Cryptography"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Cryptography safeguards data confidentiality, integrity, and authenticity using mathematical encryption methods.",
        "Digital Signatures and Public Key Infrastructure (PKI) establish non-repudiation and verify user identity.",
        "Cyber attacks range from malware, phishing, and ransomware to distributed denial-of-service (DDoS) vectors.",
        "Robust security architecture integrates tools like firewalls, IDS/IPS, and SIEM for real-time monitoring.",
        "Legal compliance in India relies heavily on the Information Technology Act, 2000 and directives from CERT-In."
      ],
      "id": "b3hkcr3"
    },
